        "body": "Serve Robotics Inc. is a public company headquartered in San Carlos, California, trading under the ticker SERV, with CIK 0001832483. According to its website, it builds self-driving robots for last-mile delivery, framing the case for them with the question, \"Why move a 2-pound burrito in a 2-ton car?\" The company describes its robots as a low-emissions solution to the last-mile problem and says it is setting the standard for safety on and beyond the sidewalk, protecting customer data, employees, and the public. It also calls itself a pop culture icon and names its robot Saymo, which it says appeared as John Mulaney's sidekick on the show \"Everybody's Live.\"\n\nThe held facts record no tracked products and no MCP servers for the company. No individual lawsuits are listed, though its recorded law exposure is in California with a count of 220.",
